course: dictionary
lesson: 7997
title: Words that mean a little bit
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The ending -ish can turn a colour word into one that means a little, or nearly. Reddish means a little red, or nearly red, but not completely red. «The American robin has a grey back and a reddish breast.» The breast is not bright red. It has some red in it.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «The African forest buffalo is a smaller, reddish cousin of the savanna buffalo» tells you the buffalo's colour is red-tinged. A reddish sky or a reddish glow is a colour somewhere between red and something else.
explain: Scientists use -ish words for colours that are not pure: reddish, greenish, bluish. «TRAPPIST-1, a small, cool, reddish star» tells you the star has a red tint, but it is not a pure, bright red.
fact: Reddish means a little red, or nearly red, but not completely.
fact: The ending -ish can mean "a bit like": reddish, greenish, bluish.
fact: «Reddish-brown» joins two colours with a hyphen: the coat is mostly brown, with some red in it.
fact: Mars is called the Red Planet because of its reddish soil.
fact: A good check is to swap in "a little red" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The American robin has a grey back and a reddish breast.» What does reddish mean here? | Blue like the sky | Shiny and wet | *Not quite red, but with a little red in it | Bright, pure red all over
exercise: «Mars is called the Red Planet for its reddish soil.» What colour is the soil? | Bright green | *A little red, but not completely red | Pure, deep black | Shining silver
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means a little red: «The reddish glow faded slowly as night came.» | faded | night | glow | *reddish
test: «The sky turned reddish as the sun went down.» What does reddish tell you about the sky? | White and cloudy | *Red-tinged, a little red but not fully red | Pure, deep red all over | Dark blue
test: Why do scientists say reddish, greenish or bluish? | *To describe colours that are not pure | To describe sounds that are loud | To describe food that tastes sweet | To describe things that are heavy
exam: What is the best meaning of reddish? | Hot like fire | *A little red, or nearly red, but not completely | Blue like the sky | Very red and bright
